el that too well one of  the factors that we  felt was necessary for us to look at  was whether there were aspects of the  way things are dealt with at the moment  which um did not assist complainers  to move on from having the experience  that they'd had  and which were capable of  re-traumatization  one of the most common uh issues that  arose in that discussion was that  people felt having to tell their  give their account repeatedly was  something which  was capable of re-traumatizing them and  so  we looked at whether we could start from  a position  that a court would adopt  trauma-centered trauma-based  approaches which would uh avoid that  and we've seen such an outpouring of you  know grief and anger after the  sarah everard's um death um in the uk  um do you feel that now is the time to  really start seriously looking  in scotland but also in other parts of  the uk as well about how we deal with  these  crimes against women girls well  obviously  cases of of murder would not be  part of the remit of our  review we were dealing only with sexual  offences  but one of the things that drove the  review was  the feeling that it was necessary to  look at  how these cases as a whole were managed  and that we could do better and if you  look at the conviction rates for rape  and also sexual offences  they've always been pretty low and it  feels like they're getting worse i mean  certainly  in england and wales over the last three  years rape convictions more than  halved do you think things are getting  worse  well we didn't proceed on the basis that  the conviction rate was a driving factor  in our report we proceeded  on the basis that what was necessary was  to find a better way of managing the  cases that  avoided traumatization we very  specifically  decided that we should not approach  matters on the basis that was any kind  of  appropriate conviction rate  or that convictions should be a marker  of success  so we adopted a completely different  approach which was simply to look  at the experience of those who were  complaining of sexual violence women or  men  has it been quite hard in your career to  have seen the impact  on some of these people who do come  forward yes some of the uh accounts  that we had uh that explained that  people  felt re-traumatized after their  engagement with the criminal justice  system  was one that was difficult for us to to  to hear because  clearly that is not the intention and  we had to listen to that and find a way  of  creating a system that would not do that  do you feel that rape has been  effectively decriminalized in the uk  because of the low conviction rates  uh i i don't think that's something that  was within the review  groups uh remit or that i can comment on  it's a crime that's taken very seriously  and it continues to be taken very  seriously and  this review shows how seriously we  intend to take it  okay thank you so much and thank you so  much for coming on and explaining some  of the details about the review as well
 

